course: dictionary
lesson: 10224
title: Toady: a creep who flatters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A toady is someone who flatters a powerful person too much and obeys them, to get favours. As a verb, «He toadied to the boss» means he behaved like a toady. In everyday speech, a toady is a creep.
explain: Context helps. In «The stoats call "It will be your head next time, Toady!" and laugh», the stoats are bullies, so their laughing is not friendly. Ask yourself: who is trying to win favour, and from whom? If someone is flattering a powerful person to get something, you are close to toady.
explain: Be careful with names. In The Wind in the Willows, the character Toad is called Toady, but he is not a toady himself. He is proud and boastful. The weasels and stoats flatter him only when it suits them, so the toady behaviour belongs to them.
fact: A toady is a person who flatters and obeys a powerful person too much, to get favours.
fact: «Toady» can also be a verb: «He toadied to the boss» means he behaved like a toady.
fact: Informally, a toady is a creep.
fact: The word may come from old travelling sellers' helpers who pretended to eat «poisonous» toads.
fact: In a rare sense, toady means like a toad.
exercise: «He toadied to the boss.» What does toadied mean? | Ran a race with the boss | *Flattered and obeyed the boss to get favours | Hid from the boss | Shouted at the boss
exercise: The king's helpers agreed with every word he said and laughed at all his jokes, even the bad ones. What are these helpers called? | Farmers | Poets | *Toadies | Travellers
exercise: Which informal word means a toady, a person who flatters to get favours? | Ancient | Glum | *A creep | Barely
test: «The stoats laughed till they nearly had two fits.» Here, a fit means what? | A piece of furniture | *A sudden attack of laughing | A shape that fits neatly | A sports match
test: Which sentence shows a toady at work? | "I disagree, and here is why." | "The weather is cold today." | *"You are right about everything, your Majesty!" | "Let us go to the river."
exam: Which word means a person who flatters a powerful person too much to get favours? | Ancient | Glum | *Barely | Toady
